  "body": "Fetch already supports setting referrerPolicy.\r\nBut as you know, Fetch is not always a better API than XHR for AJAX, such as progress updating, etc.\r\nSo adding support for referrerPolicy in XHR will be helpful.\r\n\r\nSo far I can only come up with an ugly workaround to support standalone referrerPolicy for every XHR request ---- just create a tag `<meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"{any referrerPolicy you want}\">`, and insert it into DOM before sending an XHR request, then remove this `<meta>` to clean up.\r\nBut the global Referrer-Policy setting of the page will not be restored as it was after the `<meta>` being removed. I tested it on Chrome 87.",
